WEBVTT

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.070
<i>What's Kuro-senpai doing here?</i>

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.420
<i>His steps are so clumsy.</i>

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.100
<i>He basically has no sports 
or martial arts experience,</i>

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.420
<i>yet he looks completely unfazed 
taking that monster on.</i>

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.700
<i>That's undoubtedly Kuro-senpai.</i>

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.850
<i>I figured something like this might 
happen, but right now? Really?</i>

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.430
Hey!

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.850
What the hell do you 
think you're doing?!

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.270
You have a monster summon me and then 
leave the place we're supposed to meet,

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.590
and you leave a ghost with a message?!

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.960
<i>Why couldn't you have just 
waited at the restaurant?</i>

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.490
Say someth—

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.210
Hey, we need to save him.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.460
We can leave him alone. He'll be fine.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:09.150
I'm sure even he's prepared to have 
his head smashed in at least once.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:09.890
Huh?!

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.260
K...

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:19.500
Kuro-kun!

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.520
Why is Kuro-kun...

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.800
If you get any closer, 
you might get caught in the middle.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.610
Let's just watch for a bit.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.470
But it looks like he could 
go down at any moment.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:09.710
He's tripping over his own feet!

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.900
Yes, but it doesn't seem like 
she's that much stronger than he is.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.290
It should be simple, then.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.570
Especially if he's willing to 
take a steel beam to the face.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.830
Even if he's close to death,

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.180
he'll be able to get back up immediately

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.210
thanks to the immortality he gained 
by eating mermaid flesh.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:04.300
Is this the first time you've 
seen Kuro-senpai die?

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.210
Of course it is.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.060
Then why did you break up with him?

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:11.870
I saw a cut on his hand 
disappear immediately.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.830
I saw his severed fingers grow back.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:19.650
And yet Kuro-kun acted like 
nothing even happened.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.330
Well, he <i>is</i> immortal. You should expect that.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.160
<i>An able-bodied boyfriend.</i>

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.080
<i>Couldn't she just accept that he 
would've made a great husband?</i>

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.160
<i>That she'd never have to worry 
about him being injured or sick?</i>

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.670
<i>The way she's acting now, I guess not.</i>

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:38.030
Is it so strange to suddenly 
feel scared at the thought

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:40.170
of becoming family with someone like that?

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.130
Am I not allowed to reconsider marriage?

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:49.350
Dozens of his relatives and extended family 
have died of illness or unusual causes.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.570
Kuro-kun's the only one living a decent life.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.020
Looks like Kuro-senpai's back.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:23.780
I-If he gets that close, 
he's going to get killed again!

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:42.480
<i>He stopped right before the 
steel beam could hit him.</i>

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:48.190
<i>Kuro-kun and Steel Lady Nanase look 
like they're following a script.</i>

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:50.490
<i>Everything seems calculated.</i>

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:53.210
I can't believe he grabbed her so easily...

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:57.500
Well, Steel Lady Nanase is mostly just 
swinging the steel beam without thinking.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.290
The probability of something like 
this happening is rather high.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:04.250
And if it's likely to happen,

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.870
it's not hard for Kuro-senpai 
to set that future in stone.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:12.760
That's another one of 
Kuro-senpai's abilities.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:14.390
The powers of the prophet beast,

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.160
the kudan, whose flesh he ate 
along with the mermaid's.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:19.100
The ability to determine the future.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:23.780
<i>He said that he hadn't 
told Saki-san everything</i>

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.860
<i>about the secrets of the Sakuragawa family.</i>

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:34.700
<i>It all started ten odd generations 
before Kuro-senpai, with the head of</i>

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.910
<i>the Sakuragawa family at that time.</i>

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:42.460
If your liver is bad, eat the liver 
of a creature with a strong one.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:46.420
If your eyes are bad, eat the eyes 
of a creature with good vision.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:49.570
Then, perhaps, if you ate the flesh of a kudan,

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:52.430
you could acquire its prophetic powers!

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.850
If I could freely see into the future,

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.810
I could gain an unfathomable 
amount of wealth and knowledge!

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.810
<b>Kudan</b>

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:00.150
<i>The kudan.</i>

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:06.620
<i>A yokai with the head of a 
human and the body of a cow.</i>

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:10.320
<i>It can speak human language, 
and once it predicts the future, it dies.</i>

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.030
<i>On occasion, it would predict good futures,</i>

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:15.580
<i>such as a good harvest or 
prosperity for a family,</i>

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:19.580
<i>but most of its predictions would be 
misfortunes, and they were 100% accurate.</i>

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:24.330
<i>He got his hands on kudan meat and 
had several in his household eat it.</i>

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.840
<i>Some died instantly after having 
a bad reaction to the meat.</i>

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.340
<i>Some died after being 
bedridden for a month.</i>

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.430
<i>And others died after 
they predicted the future.</i>

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:37.850
<i>They say those predictions 
turned out to be accurate.</i>

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:41.750
<i>The head of the household 
continued this over and over.</i>

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:46.610
<i>But even those who obtained the ability 
to see the future died immediately...</i>

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:49.070
<i>Just like the kudan.</i>

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:56.580
I'm so close... I'm so close, and now...

00:07:58.270 --> 00:07:59.580
Damn it!

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.970
<i>And then he realized...</i>

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:14.220
<b>Mermaid</b>

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:11.890
<i>Those with the ability to predict</i>

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:14.220
<i>the future just needed 
to have immortal bodies.</i>

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:17.390
<i>So then he started having people consume</i>

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:20.220
<i>mermaid flesh along with the kudan meat.</i>

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:24.440
<i>But the number of victims skyrocketed,</i>

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:28.460
<i>and the experiment never worked.</i>

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:36.490
<i>Time passed, and such nightmarish 
experiments were forgotten.</i>

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:37.810
<i>But...</i>

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:39.230
Kuro.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:42.960
Grandmother.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.030
Dinner is ready.

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:45.710
Okay.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:47.960
Let's eat.

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:01.490
Nii-san?

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:03.270
What?

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.940
Grandmother, they're all...

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.280
Th-They all seem to be in pain!

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:23.040
Ah, Kuro...

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:26.040
You feel completely fine?

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.630
Do you have a fever? 
Do you feel nauseous?

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.000
No, I'm fine...

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:33.270
It's come true! It's finally come true!

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:36.760
<i>His grandmother was 
still chasing the dream.</i>

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:40.430
<i>She had been secretly gathering 
kudan meat and mermaid flesh.</i>

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:43.010
Grandmother.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:45.900
They're suffering. Please help them!

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.520
Let's see...

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:51.050
I would love to know what the 
weather will be like tomorrow.

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:51.730
Huh?

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:54.480
You should be able to tell me that, Kuro.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:57.360
I need you to die once and go see...

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.710
the future!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:06.500
<i>And then, his insane grandmother 
tried various experiments.</i>

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:10.260
<i>To see if he was immortal, 
and if he could predict the future,</i>

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:14.090
<i>she cut up his body and made him 
suffer mortal wounds repeatedly,</i>

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.830
<i>until he stopped feeling 
pain almost altogether.</i>

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:18.500
Kuro.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:26.180
There are lots of fireflies 
by the river out back.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:27.930
Want to go see them with me?

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.220
Sure.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.100
Well, come along, then.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:38.700
Is something wrong?

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:42.860
Nope. It's nothing, Nee-san.

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:45.980
The dream of the Sakuragawa 
family had finally come true.

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:50.330
But the abilities obtained were 
slightly different from what they desired.

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.090
While he is still human,

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:57.630
<i>he became something inhuman.</i>

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:36.460
Ah, Kuro-senpai...

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:39.100
The way he can do something 
like that with no hesitation

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:40.560
is another one of his charms!

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:43.770
I don't need a boyfriend who 
can snap a ghost's neck.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.600
<i>Now, this is the real question.</i>

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:50.330
<i>Will this truly be the 
end of Steel Lady Nanase?</i>

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.500
I figured that wouldn't work.

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:07.420
<i>This means we only have one option.</i>

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:17.420
Kuro-senpai, that should be enough.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:22.770
We'll need a different strategy 
to defeat Steel Lady Nanase.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:39.070
A Monster of the Imagination

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:49.050
Saki-san, what are you doing here?

00:12:50.090 --> 00:12:54.580
I work as a police officer in this city. 
What are you doing here, Kuro-kun?

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:56.580
Well...

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:01.460
Of course, if your dear girlfriend 
asks you to show up,

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:04.890
you'll show up, even if it means
fighting a monster, right?

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:09.100
Something like that.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.750
Though I wasn't informed that 
you'd be here, Saki-san.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:14.350
I also had no idea you'd 
show up, Kuro-kun.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:17.350
Well, I had no intention of 
letting you see each other.

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:21.070
So she really is your current girlfriend?

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:24.550
Yes... She really is my current girlfriend...

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:27.500
Kuro-senpai! Why do you sound 
like it absolutely pains you?!

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.200
Because it does absolutely pain me.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:33.870
I'm sorry, Saki-san. I'm pretty sure 
Iwanaga caused you some trouble.

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:38.500
Kuro-senpai! I actually saved Saki-san!

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.500
I don't deserve this kind of treatment—

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.070
Just apologize.

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:44.590
There's no way you didn't cause trouble.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:49.550
It's fine. I'm sure we both 
caused each other trouble.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:52.810
What we should be worried about 
right now is Steel Lady Nanase.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:55.540
So anyway,

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:57.690
it's good to see you, Kuro-kun.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:03.190
Yes. It's good to see you, too... Saki-san.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:09.110
Let's go somewhere else.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:12.330
Lingering in a vending machine's
 light for so long is way too sad.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.870
It's not as if we're moths!

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:18.870
<i>I knew I shouldn't have let 
these two see each other.</i>

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:23.690
<i>How did this happen?</i>

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.590
<i>It's not like we could've talked 
about this at the restaurant,</i>

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:30.970
<i>and I was scared to go home alone, but...</i>

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.350
Kuro-senpai.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.660
Why are you staring at your 
ex-girlfriend from behind

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:39.560
when your current girlfriend 
is sitting right next to you?

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:40.810
You're just imagining it.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:41.980
I am not! I just saw you!

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:45.820
"Oh, she's lost some weight. 
I hope she's been eating right.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.740
I wonder if she looks like 
skin and bones because of me.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.730
Wow, her hips look nice, though."

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:53.530
I know that's you were thinking.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:57.150
I'm impressed. 
That's exactly what I was thinking.

00:14:57.150 --> 00:14:58.610
Saki-san's beautiful.

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:01.120
Don't admit that! 
How dare you admit that so quickly?!

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:03.980
And how dare you take that 
attitude with me after

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:06.290
leaving your poor girlfriend 
alone for a whole week?!

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.950
Why didn't you reply to any of my messages?

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:12.670
Oh, so those were from you. 
I thought they were spam messages.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:14.960
At least look at me!

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:16.490
I see you two get along great.

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:18.140
Of course we do!

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.650
Just so you know, we're usually 
even more lovey-dovey!

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:26.880
Saki-san, are you still not 
able to eat fish or beef?

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:29.600
I can eat some now.

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:31.360
My job is the reason I lost weight.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:33.870
I'm sorry.

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:36.620
Again, this isn't your fault, Kuro-kun.

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:39.350
<i>We broke up without straightening things out,</i>

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:41.910
<i>so I thought I'd be more 
shaken up if I saw him.</i>

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:44.880
<i>I wonder if I'm able to stay 
so calm because of her.</i>

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:51.380
Anyway, let's get to the matter at hand.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:54.310
<i>Though she's still pretty intolerable...</i>

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:55.890
Yes, you're right.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:01.510
Kuro-kun, were you fighting Steel Lady 
Nanase on orders from Iwanaga-san?

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:02.390
Uh...

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:09.460
I did come to Makurazaka City 
because she called me,

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:11.860
but I just happened to run 
into Steel Lady Nanase.

00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:13.420
When I got to the station,

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:16.530
a goblin cat that had been attacked by 
Steel Lady Nanase came to me for help.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:23.460
These creatures would usually do 
everything they can to avoid me,

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:25.670
but after spending so much time with Iwanaga,

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:28.250
they started to see me as 
someone they could rely on

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:32.730
in place of their lady 
of one eye and one leg,

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:35.300
and started asking me for help, as well.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:38.560
I didn't have time to contact Iwanaga,

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:42.460
so I went to where Steel Lady 
Nanase appeared by myself.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.070
Oh, that's good.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:49.390
Maybe the kappa won't run 
away from you next time.

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:52.100
Having them rely on me all 
the time isn't much better.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:56.490
More importantly, Steel Lady Nanase 
didn't fear me when she saw me.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:17:00.730
Well, Kuro-san <i>does</i> look like 
a horrifying, evil, jumbled mess

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:06.060
of a creature that's some unsightly 
mix of a human, mermaid,

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:08.630
and kudan to those who aren't human.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:11.430
Apparently, even the monsters 
consider him a monster.

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:12.010
Huh?

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:14.790
Then, Iwanaga-san,

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:18.970
what does that make Steel Lady Nanase, 
since she doesn't react to Kuro-kun?

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:20.970
She's a monster.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:25.770
Well, I can see that. Let me rephrase. 
Is she something that can be exterminated?

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:26.940
She is.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:30.400
The reason I wanted to see you 
tonight is to discuss that.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.400
Steel Lady Nanase is different 
from a normal spectre.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:37.410
She was created from the delusions 
and desires of modern-day humans.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:39.780
She's a monster of the imagination.

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:44.310
<i>I hadn't planned to tell her 
all of this, but at this point,</i>

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:46.130
<i>I'll tell her as much of the truth</i>

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:50.170
<i>as I can so she'll understand how 
different our world is from hers.</i>

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:55.670
<i>I'll show her just how different 
we are. That's the best plan.</i>

00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:00.830
The yokai, monsters, ghosts, mononoke, and beasts from urban legends

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.530
that we're familiar with

00:18:02.530 --> 00:18:06.300
have monsters of the imagination 
hidden among them.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:08.440
It may start as something trivial.

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:10.590
For example, someone might say...

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:13.770
A creepy pale lady wearing 
a mask came up to me,

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:15.610
but she was scary, so I ran away.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:17.500
That's how the story would start.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.100
Huh? And then?

00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:22.880
But that's not a very interesting story, so...

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:24.880
And when I took a closer look,

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:26.890
I realized her mouth was 
split open under the mask.

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:28.460
I got scared, so I ran away,

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:30.990
but then she came running 
after me as fast as she could.

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:32.710
Wow, that's really scary.

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:35.680
And now there's a lie added to the story.

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:38.220
Eventually, that story will spread.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:40.400
A woman wearing a mask...

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:42.280
...asked, "Am I pretty?"

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:44.290
Under the mask, her mouth was...

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:45.900
Under the mask, her mouth was...

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:50.230
This is all still just a story.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:54.230
It becomes a problem when 
this is given a name.

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:57.550
The slit-mouth woman.

00:18:58.420 --> 00:19:01.080
They give that story a single name

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.620
that manages to generally 
describe what it looks like.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:08.810
That puts together all of these 
vague rumors and solidifies them

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:11.090
into a uniform image.

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:15.130
At first, it was just make-believe,

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:18.170
but now that the fiction 
has a name and a shape,

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:21.090
it implants itself into the minds 
of thousands, tens of thousands,

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:23.790
and millions of people's minds,

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:28.140
which gives it flesh and blood, 
turning it into something real.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:31.310
People's imaginations manage 
to create a monster.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:35.900
Do you expect anyone to believe 
this happens every day?

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.630
Are you really asking that after 
seeing a kappa and a ghost?

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:43.910
Usually, monsters of the 
imagination are nothing to fear.

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:45.710
They're popular for a short time,

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:47.410
and even if they gain a form, they're weak.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:50.410
They usually disappear soon after.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:54.540
The slit-mouth woman and human-faced 
dog eventually disappeared.

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.670
But in that case, isn't Steel Lady Nanase

00:19:57.060 --> 00:20:00.130
rather different from the monster 
of the imagination that you speak of?

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:04.480
It's been given the name 
"Steel Lady Nanase,"

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:06.640
but she's so powerful.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:07.890
Yes, exactly that.

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:08.890
Huh?

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:13.170
Why did it manage to gain a form not 
even a year after Nanase Karin's death

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:15.650
and become that powerful?

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:17.900
There is a way to make that possible.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:21.610
Usually, rumors take time to spread.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.470
So what can spread them instantly

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:25.410
where countless eyes can see them?

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:29.370
Only certain media outlets even 
bothered reporting the accident.

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:32.210
It's really only popular on the Internet...

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:38.000
Exactly. The culprit is the Internet.

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:41.980
The Internet can relay information 
all around the world in an instant,

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:44.760
and many people have access to it.

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:50.270
And it's able to gather an endless 
amount of varying ideas in one place.

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:52.030
In one place?

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:55.270
Oh, like that Steel Lady Nanase wiki?

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:58.500
Ah, so you know of it. 
That'll make this easier.

00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:02.030
That site is the reason her name 
and description have been defined,

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.090
and why it spread at such an alarming rate.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.240
And the illustration of 
her on the top page...

00:21:09.340 --> 00:21:12.160
That gave her a from that's 
hard to get from rumors alone

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:15.500
and defined what she should 
look like in an instant.

00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:17.960
Do you remember what 
the picture looks like?

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.460
Yes.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.570
Don't you think that 
the Steel Lady Nanase

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:25.010
on that page looked exactly like the 
one we saw, down to the finest detail?

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.930
Now that you mention it, yes. 
What about it, though?

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:30.390
Do you think it's really possible

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:32.430
to illustrate a ghost made up of rumors

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:35.690
so precisely, when there's never 
been a solid eyewitness report?

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:37.770
Of course you can't.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:39.190
What happened is the opposite.

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:40.690
The opposite?

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:44.190
That drawing wasn't 
modeled after the ghost.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:47.260
But because so many people 
imagined Steel Lady Nanase

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:49.520
to look like that from that illustration,

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:52.100
it took that form.

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:55.580
Huh?

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.610
Everything is backwards.

00:21:57.610 --> 00:22:00.840
The wiki wasn't created 
because there was a ghost.

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:05.090
The ghost was born because 
the wiki was created.

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:08.090
<b>Steel Lady Nanase Wiki</b>

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:08.090
You could call this website

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:12.100
the true identity of Steel Lady Nanase.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:16.370
To Be Continued

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:47.020
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:48.780
Steel Lady Nanase maintains 
her immortal form thanks to

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:49.910
many people's imaginations.

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:51.060
To defeat her,

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:54.410
we need to think up a story that'll 
surpass an actual story of a spectre.

00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:56.910
The thing we need to face her head-on is...

00:23:56.910 --> 00:23:59.070
Next time, "Logical Fiction."
